     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum daily dose, and each dose is double the maximum single dose. Ibuprofen has a ceiling effect for analgesia and anti-inflammatory action, so doses above the maximum add no benefit. They do raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. I can't identify a clinical scenario where this dose would help the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a specific indication that calls for a higher dose, a clinical pharmacist consult is the best next step. If the dose is still needed after that, it would need to go through your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nIf you want one of the options above, tell me which and I'll enter it."
      }
